.TH qsh-setup-listener 1  "listener 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-setup\-listener \- This machine runs `qsh listen` for a reverse peer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh setup listener\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-service\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
This machine runs `qsh listen` for a reverse peer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The peer\*(Aqs trust\-store name
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-peer\-cert\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Pin the peer from its certificate file (`\-` reads standard input)
.TP
\fB\-\-service\fR
Also write the service unit file
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
